{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.MassGapObstruction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MassGapObstruction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Torsion.MassGap","lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.qou_obstruction_reduction","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.IntervalCases"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.massgap_classical_limit_obstruction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.massgap_classical_limit_obstruction","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MassGapObstruction.lean#L83-L106","doc":"**Step 3, mass-gap arm (combined statement).**  Conditional on the\nobstruction-reduction context with χ(A) = −6:\n\n1. the categorical gap bound vanishes at the classical point\n   `q = 1` (unconditional — `QOU.Torsion.massGapBound_at_one`);\n2. the Kummer obstruction persists at every prime `p > 3`.\n\nTogether: the mass-gap classical limit and the classical-limit\nobstruction both reduce to the divisibility structure of\nχ(A) = −6 in the Kummer tower — the gap's death at `q = 1` is the\nμ₂ face (`2 ∣ 6`, `kummer_vanishes_at_two`) of the same class\nwhose primes-above-3 faces obstruct the classical limit.\n\nSee the module docstring for the mandatory universality caveat:\nthis is a statement about the QOU framework's classical limit,\nconditional on `QouObstructionReductionContext`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.kummer_persists_above_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.kummer_persists_above_three","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MassGapObstruction.lean#L67-L81","doc":"**Kummer persistence above 3 at χ(A) = −6** — the obstruction\ndoes NOT vanish at any prime `p > 3`: such a prime does not\ndivide 6.  This is the workplan's \"the classical-limit\nobstruction persists at all primes > 3\" as a theorem. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.kummer_vanishes_at_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.kummer_vanishes_at_two","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MassGapObstruction.lean#L55-L65","doc":"**Kummer level-2 vanishing at χ(A) = −6** — the Kummer shadow of\nthe μ₂-vanishing of the gap: `2 ∣ 6`, so the level-2 obstruction\nclass vanishes, matching the (unconditional) vanishing of the\ncategorical gap bound at the classical point. ","signatureChunk":0}]}